<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How calculator inputs, private contact messages, editor sessions, sponsored links and hosting request information are handled by this website."><div class="shell page-intro legal"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Privacy'}]}/><h1>Privacy policy</h1><div class="prose"><p>Updated 13 November 2026. This notice describes the implemented website. The operator must review its identity, applicable requirements and provider settings before the final public launch.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Calculations run on your device. The public calculator does not send its numeric inputs to a server, store them in local storage, or require a visitor account.</p><h2>Private contact messages</h2><p>The contact form collects the name, reply email, subject and message you submit, plus your acknowledgment of this notice. It sends those fields over HTTPS to a private inbox available to the authenticated owner. Message bodies are encrypted by the application before storage in the site's dedicated Cloudflare D1 database; decryption requires a separate Worker secret. They are not committed to the website's GitHub source repository.</p><p>Messages remain available in the inbox for 30 days. Daily cleanup removes expired records within the following 24 hours, so live storage may retain them for up to 31 days. Provider backups and infrastructure retention follow the operator's Cloudflare settings and provider policies. Archiving changes the inbox view; it does not extend retention. Do not send passwords, access tokens, financial details or other sensitive information.</p><p>The form uses a short-lived timing token, an empty honeypot field and request rate limits to reduce abuse. Request IP information is used for rate limiting; the application does not store it alongside contact messages. A receipt confirms storage, not an email delivery, response time or promised reply. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> for a privacy or correction request and include the receipt reference where relevant.</p><h2>Editor authentication</h2><p>The private dashboard verifies the approved editor's email and password over HTTPS. It stores a salted password verifier and a separate signing key, not the original password. Signed sessions use a Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookie lasting up to eight hours. Login attempts are rate limited. Editorial source and commit history are stored in the owner's GitHub repository.</p><h2 id="analytics">Google Analytics</h2><p>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand visits to public pages. The Google tag loads on public pages without a consent banner. Calculator values and contact messages are not sent.</p><p>Google receives page-view and engagement information, a pseudonymous browser identifier, browser/device information and network information such as your IP address during transmission. The integration sends page URLs without query strings or fragments and limits referrer information to its origin. Calculator numeric inputs, contact-message fields and dashboard activity are not intentionally sent to Analytics. Advertising personalization and Google signals are disabled in the site tag. Enhanced measurement is disabled for this stream so forms, searches and outbound URLs are not automatically tracked.</p><p>Analytics cookies may last up to 180 days as configured by the site tag. Google processing and account-level retention follow the Analytics property settings and Google's policies; information already received by Google is not erased by blocking it in your browser. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">Google Analytics data safeguards</a>. Blocking Analytics does not prevent use of the calculators or contact form.</p><h2>Sponsored banners</h2><p>If enabled, sponsored image or text banners are labeled and use sponsored links. Following a source or sponsored link opens an independently operated service with its own privacy practices.</p><h2>Website performance measurements</h2><p>Cloudflare Web Analytics measures public-page loading and browser performance, including timing and device/browser information. It is separate from Google Analytics and does not receive calculator input values or contact-message fields from our application. See <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/data-origin-and-collection/">Cloudflare's description of performance data collection</a>. Private dashboard responses restrict external analytics scripts.</p><h2>Hosting requests</h2><p>Cloudflare receives request information such as IP address, requested URL and browser headers when serving or securing the website. Logging, security processing, data location, backups and retention depend on provider behavior and account configuration. Read <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for provider information.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>New analytics, advertising networks, message-delivery providers or data uses would require a corresponding policy review. This page does not claim that provider settings or legal compliance have been independently certified.</p></div></div></Base>
